 ## Delivery
 
 `estimateDelivery(orderedAt, transitDays)` returns the expected delivery date in Istanbul time.
+
+## Invoice tax
+
+`computeInvoice(lines, { taxRatePercent, discountPercent = 0 })` in `src/tax.js` returns `{ lines, netCents, discountCents, taxCents, grossCents }`.
+
+- Each line's net is `quantity × unitCents`. A negative quantity is a credit line.
+- The invoice discount is `discountPercent` of the positive line nets, rounded half to even. It is split across the positive lines in proportion to their nets using the largest-remainder method, with ties going to the earlier line. Credit lines get no discount.
+- Each line's tax is `taxRatePercent` of its net minus its discount, rounded half to even (symmetric for negatives, so -13.5 becomes -14).
+- Percentages must be between 0 and 100 with at most two decimals. All arithmetic is exact.
